# Documentation and knowledge

Source of truth: `AGENTS.md` sections 8 and 12, `rules/knowledge-closing-check.md` and
`knowledge/README.md`.

- Read the code before documenting it; names, defaults and options are taken verbatim.
- Unknown facts stay `<placeholder>` and are asked about.
- A behaviour change updates its documentation in the same commit.
- Durable knowledge goes into `knowledge/`, never into private tool memory.
- Record only confirmed facts; mark everything else as unverified or leave it out.
- New knowledge documents start from a template in `knowledge/templates/`.
